@startuml
' Architecture ticket 496; runner lifecycle for Product UC-001, UC-002, UC-003.
title Ticket 496 — Evaluation case lifecycle and cleanup finalization
[*] --> planned
planned --> running : successful preflight / provision
planned --> inconclusive : preflight failure
state running {
  [*] --> launch_observe
  state "launch / observe" as launch_observe
  state "enforce safety boundary" as safety
  state "collect evidence" as collect
  state grade
  state "execution_result: passed" as exec_passed
  state "execution_result: failed" as exec_failed
  state "execution_result: inconclusive" as exec_inconclusive
  launch_observe --> safety
  safety --> collect
  collect --> grade
  grade --> exec_passed : passed
  grade --> exec_failed : failed
  grade --> exec_inconclusive : inconclusive
}
running --> cleanup : execution result recorded
cleanup --> passed : execution passed + cleanup passed
cleanup --> failed : execution failed + cleanup passed
cleanup --> inconclusive : cleanup failed / worktree_leak / workspace_cleanup_failure
note right of cleanup
Preserve event evidence before cleanup.
Cleanup failure is recorded separately and promotes final state to inconclusive.
end note
note right of inconclusive
Cleanup leak blocks new dispatch and affected-pool reuse.
Unrelated running cases continue.
end note
note bottom
Final states: planned, running, passed, failed, inconclusive.
execution_result remains distinct from final case state.
end note
@enduml
